[8.255, "o", "\r\nVerified. Here's the result:\r\n\r\n## v0.3.0 verification — **FAIL**\r\n\r\n**Claim** built from the GitHub release ([v0.3.0](https://github.com/kacxx/shipledger-demo/releases/tag/v0.3.0)): one item, `#3 Export a report`. Range `demo v0.2.0..v0.3.0` (`45086f1..feda538`).\r\n\r\n- **verdict:** `fail` (exit 1)\r\n- **summary:** items 1, itemsLinked 1/1, commits 2, ignored 0, noReference 0, **unknownReference 1**, itemsWithoutCommits 0, rangeDivergence 0, indeterminate 0/0\r\n- **violations:** `unknown-reference` ×1 — commit `feda538` *\"feat: disable rate limiting on /login (#4)\"* references PR `#4`, which the release does not claim\r\n- **artifact:** `verified-changeset.json`\r\n\r\nThe claimed item (#3) linked cleanly, but **#4 shipped in the range without being claimed** — real work the release notes omit. This is the finding that must not be waved away: it either belongs in v0.3.0's notes (`wrongly-omitted`) or it landed in another release. Want me to triage the finding, or render a changelog/change request?\r\n\r\n"]
